   "id": "niddah.19b.4",
   "daf": "19b",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "וַחֲכָמִים מְטַהֲרִין. הַיְינוּ תַּנָּא קַמָּא! אִיכָּא בֵינַיְיהוּ לִתְלוֹת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states with regard to blood that is green: «And the Rabbis deem» it «pure.» The Gemara asks: «Isn’t this» opinion of the Rabbis identical to the opinion of «the first tanna?» The Gemara answers: «There is» a practical difference «between them» with regard to whether «to leave in abeyance» blood that is green. According to the first tanna of the mishna there are five types of blood that are definitely impure, whereas other types, such as green, are impure due to uncertainty. By contrast, the Rabbis maintain that green blood is entirely pure."
  }
